Subject: Port: the test builds' autopilot plays through the pads
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Test builds (MSCHARGED_AUTOPILOT) can hand the first local player to a bot:
C, P and U held together in the game window. The bot is the port's
src/platform/autopilot.cpp; release builds link an empty one.

It plays the way a person does, with the player's Remote and Nunchuk. Each
fixed step reads the pads (UpdatePlatPad) before the pads take the status
(PadManager::Update) and the step captures its inputs; between the two, the
bot may write that player's buttons, stick and shakes into the step's status.
So the inputs the step captures and the network sends, what the rollback
predicts and keeps, and the reads of the local pad itself (the Mega Strike
meter, the goalie's pointer) are all its presses as a player's: nothing on
either machine can tell, and no other code changes. Steps the rollback runs
again read no pads, so the bot plays each step once.

Add include/mscharged_autopilot.h, its interface to the port.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_autopilot.h b/include/mscharged_autopilot.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2721ebd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/mscharged_autopilot.h
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#ifndef MSCHARGED_AUTOPILOT_H
+#define MSCHARGED_AUTOPILOT_H
+
+// The test builds' autopilot (the port's src/platform/autopilot.cpp; C, P and
+// U together in the game window; release builds have an empty one).
+struct PlatPadManager;
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// After a fixed step's pad read, before the pads take it: may write the first
+// local player's Remote and Nunchuk status in `manager`.
+void mscharged_tweak_step_pads(struct PlatPadManager* manager);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif // MSCHARGED_AUTOPILOT_H
+#endif // MSCHARGED_TWEAKS
diff --git a/src/Game/Task/FixedUpdateTask.cpp b/src/Game/Task/FixedUpdateTask.cpp
index ff3be53..34bff39 100644
--- a/src/Game/Task/FixedUpdateTask.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Task/FixedUpdateTask.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
 #include "mscharged_rollback.h"
 #endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#include "mscharged_autopilot.h"
+#endif
 #include "Game/InputRouter.h"
 #include "Game/NetworkInput.h"
 #include "Game/NetworkSync.h"
@@ -393,5 +396,10 @@ void FixedUpdateTask::Run(float dt)
             g_pPadManager->SetActivePadSet(1);
             simulationTick = g_fFixedUpdateTick;
             UpdatePlatPad(g_pPlatPadManager);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+            // The test builds' autopilot plays the first local player through
+            // this step's pad status, before the pads (and the inputs) take it.
+            mscharged_tweak_step_pads(g_pPlatPadManager);
+#endif
             g_pPadManager->Update(simulationTick);
             FlickDetection::Update();
